  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "When returning RDF to clients, the complete list of namespace prefixes known to the server is included. It would save a lot of lines in the response to only include the namespace prefixes that are being used.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Note:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This doesn't appear to be something jena provides. It may require some work to inspect the stream to compare what namespaces are present versus what namespaces are being provided. I believe that would happen in the two blocks here:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-http-commons/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/http/commons/responses/RdfStreamStreamingOutput.java#L126-L147"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-http-commons/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/http/commons/responses/RdfStreamStreamingOutput.java#L126-L147",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
